#### 3.4.3 Systematic Uncertainties

The systematic uncertainties of the \(A_{LL}\) measurements for the \(\pi^{\pm}\)-tagged jets include the following sources:

* Uncertainty from the beam polarization
* Uncertainty from the particle identification
* Uncertainty for the relative luminosity \(R_{3}\)
* Uncertainty from the trigger bias
* Uncertainty from the underlying event correction

#### 1. Uncertainty from the Beam Polarization

As described in Sec. 2.1.3, the relative uncertainty of the beam polarization is about 6.06%. This uncertainty will contribute to all data points as an overall scale uncertainty.

#### 2. Uncertainty from the Particle Identification (PID)

As mentioned in Sec. 3.1.2, the particle fraction is fitted with different functions. The \(A_{LL}\) results have been calculated with the different fitting results and the differences have been taken as the systematic uncertainties in PID. This part is negligible in this analysis.

#### 3. Uncertainties from Relative Luminosity

According to Eq. (3.5), the longitudinal double spin asymmetry of the \(\pi^{\pm}\)-tagged jet is extracted with the following formula:

\[A_{LL}=\frac{1}{P_{Y}P_{B}}\frac{N^{+}-R_{3}N^{-}}{N^{+}+R_{3}N^{-}}, \tag{3.15}\]

where \(N^{+}=N^{++}+N^{+-}\) and \(N^{+}=N^{-+}+N^{--}\). Let \(f\equiv N^{+}/N^{-}\), and the above equation can be written as:

\[A_{LL}=\frac{1}{P_{Y}P_{B}}\frac{f-R_{3}}{f+R_{3}} \tag{3.16}\]

and \(f\) can be expressed as:

\[f=\frac{1+P_{Y}P_{B}A_{LL}}{1-P_{Y}P_{B}A_{LL}}R_{3} \tag{3.17}\]The uncertainties of \(A_{LL}\) contributed from \(R_{3}\) can be expressed as:

\[\Delta A_{LL} =|\frac{\partial A_{LL}}{\partial R_{3}}|\Delta R_{3} \tag{3.18}\] \[=\frac{1}{P_{Y}P_{B}}\frac{2f}{(f+R_{3})^{2}}\Delta R_{3}\] (3.19) \[=\frac{1}{P_{Y}P_{B}}\frac{1-(P_{Y}P_{B}A_{LL})^{2}}{2}\frac{ \Delta R_{3}}{R_{3}} \tag{3.20}\]

Since \(P_{Y}\) and \(P_{B}\) are less than 1 and \(A_{LL}\sim 10^{-2}\), the term \((P_{Y}P_{B}A_{LL})^{2}\ll 1\) and can be neglected. Therefore, the uncertainty of \(A_{LL}\) contributed from the relative luminosity \(R_{3}\) can be calculated with the following formula:

\[\Delta A_{LL}=\frac{1}{P_{Y}P_{B}}\frac{\Delta R_{3}}{2R_{3}}, \tag{3.21}\]

where \(\Delta R_{3}\) is the systematic uncertainty of the \(R_{3}\) described in Sec. 2.3.3. The calculated uncertainty contributed from \(R_{3}\) is 0.00076. This uncertainty is shared with each measured \(A_{LL}\) data points.

## 4 Uncertainties from Underlying Event Correction

Similar to Ref. [53], the contribution from the underlying event correction is estimated with the average spin-independent underlying event correction \(\langle dp_{T}\rangle\) and the double spin asymmetry \(A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}\) of the underlying event correction in data. The \(A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}\) is calculated with the following formula:

\[A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}=\frac{1}{P_{A}P_{B}}\frac{\left(\langle dp_{T}\rangle^{++}+ \langle dp_{T}\rangle^{--}\right)-\left(\langle dp_{T}\rangle^{+-}+\langle dp _{T}\rangle^{-+}\right)}{\left(\langle dp_{T}\rangle^{++}+\langle dp_{T} \rangle^{--}\right)+\left(\langle dp_{T}\rangle^{+-}+\langle dp_{T}\rangle^{ -+}\right)}, \tag{3.22}\]

where, for example, \(\langle dp_{T}\rangle^{++}\) is the average underlying event correction for the '++' beam helicity configuration. The \(A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}\) is calculated at each jet \(p_{T}\) bin in a fill-by-fill basis. Figure 3.18 and 3.19 show the calculated fill-by-fill \(A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}\) results. The \(A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}\) results as a function of jet \(p_{T}\) are presented in the bottom right panels and are fitted with a constant function. The fitting results have been used to calculated systematic uncertainties \(\delta A_{LL}^{UE}\) originating from \(A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}\) with the following formula:

\[\delta A_{LL}^{UE}=\frac{\int_{p_{T}^{min}-\langle dp_{T}\rangle A_{LL}^{dp_{ T}}}^{p_{max}-\langle dp_{T}\rangle A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}}\frac{d\sigma}{dp_{T}}dp_{T}- \int_{p_{T}^{min}+\langle dp_{T}\rangle A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}}^{p_{max}+\langle dp _{T}\rangle A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}}\frac{d\sigma}{dp_{T}}dp_{T}}{\int_{p_{T}^{min}- \langle dp_{T}\rangle A_{LL}^{dp_{T}}}^{p_{max}-\langle dp_{T}\rangle A_{LL}^ {dp_{T}}}\frac{d\sigma}{dp_{T}}dp_{T}}, \tag{3.23}\]where \(p_{T}^{max}\) and \(p_{T}^{min}\) are the upper and lower edge of a jet \(p_{T}\) bin. The \(\frac{d\sigma}{dp_{T}}\) is the unpolarized jet cross section, which is taken from next-to-leading-order pQCD calculation with the CT14 pdf [135]. The numerical values of the estimated \(\delta A_{LL}^{UE}\) are summarized Tab. 3.10.

## 5 Total Systematic Uncertainties

The total systematic uncertainties \(\delta A_{LL}^{total}\), are obtained by adding the uncertainties from different sources in quadrature as they are independent. The numerical values of the systematic uncertainties of each sources and the total uncertainties assigned to the final \(A_{LL}\) measurements are summarized in Tab. 3.11 and 3.12 for jet momentum fraction \(z>0.2\) and \(z>0.3\), respectively.

