### \(A_{ll}\) Extraction for \(\Lambda\), \(\overline{\Lambda}\) and \(K_{S}^{0}\)

The longitudinal double spin asymmetry \(A_{LL}\) can be extracted with the Eq. (3.5). In the analysis, the \(A_{LL}^{raw}\) for the \(\Lambda\) hyperons and the \(K_{S}^{0}\) candidates under the mass peak and \(A_{LL}^{bkg}\) for the residual backgrounds are extracted separately. The impact of the residual backgrounds to the final \(A_{LL}\) results and the corresponding statistical uncertainties \(\delta A_{LL}\) are corrected with the following formula:

\[A_{LL} =\frac{A_{LL}^{raw}-rA_{LL}^{bkg}}{1-r}, \tag{4.2}\] \[\delta A_{LL} =\frac{\sqrt{(\delta A_{LL}^{raw})^{2}+(r\delta A_{LL}^{bkg})^{2 }}}{1-r} \tag{4.3}\]

where \(r\) is the residual background fraction under the mass peak, and is estimated with the side-band method. \(\delta A_{LL}^{raw}\) and \(\delta A_{LL}^{bkg}\) are the statistical uncertainties from mass peak and residual background. Figure 4.6, as an example, shows the \(A_{LL}^{raw}\) as a function of \(\Lambda\) hyperons and \(K_{S}^{0}\)\(p_{T}\) (first row) and jet \(p_{T}\) (second row) for \(\Lambda\), \(\overline{\Lambda}\), and \(K_{S}^{0}\). Constant fittings (red lines on Fig. 4.6) are applied to the extracted \(A_{LL}^{raw}\) and the numerical values of the fitting results are listed on the figure. The extracted numerical values of the \(A_{LL}\) and the corresponding statistical uncertainties for each \(p_{T}\) and jet \(p_{T}\) bins after the background correction are summarized in Tab. 4.6 and 4.7, respectively.

