### Results and Discussions

With the longitudinally polarized proton-proton data taken at STAR in 2015, we performed the improved measurement of the longitudinal spin transfer \(D_{LL}\) to \(\Lambda\) and \(\overline{\Lambda}\) as a function of hyperon \(p_{T}\) and the first measurement of \(D_{LL}\) as a function of the jet momentum fraction \(z\) carried by hyperons. The statistics are about 2\(-\)3 times larger than previously published measurements [90]. The first measurements of \(D_{LL}\) vs \(z\) can provide direct probe to the polarized fragmentation functions [92].

